# CODEOWNERS — who must review changes in this repository.
#
# DOW-418: review belongs to @DOWGO/dwg-reviewers, code to @DOWGO/dwg-engineers. The two teams
# are disjoint on purpose: GitHub never requests review from a pull request's own author, so the
# separation enforces itself as long as no engineer sits in dwg-reviewers.
#
# Code-owner review is required by the org branch ruleset (DOW-320). That control was inert here
# until DOW-418: this file named @DOWGO/maintainers, a team without write access, which GitHub
# silently ignores. A code owner MUST have write access to the repository.
#
# One catch-all covers every file, so every pull request gets dwg-reviewers requested
# automatically. Path-specific rules naming the same team would be no-ops — add one only when a
# path needs a *different* owner.

*  @DOWGO/dwg-reviewers
